    "result_text": "All clean. The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. Verified against the audit output: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = region `NSW` + fiscal year `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`.\n\n**What changed (kept deliberately small per file):**\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` and its getter/setter. No other method touched.\n- **`CustomerCodes.java`** \u2014 repurposed the existing `build`/`deduplicate` pair (rather than adding a new class, to avoid a file) to emit the memberId: `region + FY(2) + hash8 + Luhn(base)`, with collision handling now keyed on `getMemberId()`. The FY is derived from `BusinessDays.roll(registrationDate ?? now)` so it matches the date `@PrePersist` will store \u2014 this also fixed the initial NPE (memberId is built before persist sets the date).\n- **`CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 removed `of(Owner)` (it read `customerCode`); kept the reusable `luhn`, now used as the CHK segment.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps from the same-named entity property, so no explicit mapping was needed.\n- **`OwnerAuditListener.java`** \u2014 audit records now reference `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 one-line change: `setMemberId(CustomerCodes.build(...))`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three field schemas with a single `memberId` (drives DTO generation, so the JSON no longer exposes the old fields).\n- **`schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the column (same position, so positional `data.sql` inserts still work; widened to `VARCHAR(32)`).\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I put the new construction logic in the small `CustomerCodes`/`CheckDigit` helper classes (low surrounding complexity) rather than growing the large controller or entity, touched only one line of the big `addOwner` method, and avoided a new file by reusing the existing build/dedup pair.\n\nTwo interpretation notes on \"the fiscal-year value ... and the owner segment must all reference the memberId\": the fiscal year is now embedded as the FY segment of `memberId`, and `OwnerSegment`/`FiscalYear` derive from the same region and registration date the memberId is built from, so their outputs stay consistent with it. No existing test pins those exact values; I kept them computing consistently rather than parsing back out of the composite string, which would be higher-risk (the `-n` dedup suffix makes positional extraction fragile).",
